        <ARI_ClinicalSubtype>Autoimmune Addison&apos;s Disease - Most common form, caused by immune attack on adrenal glands.</ARI_ClinicalSubtype>
        <ARI_ClinicalSubtype>Drug-Induced Addison’s Disease - Caused by medications that affect adrenal hormone production.</ARI_ClinicalSubtype>
        <ARI_ClinicalSubtype>Genetic Addison’s Disease - Due to inherited conditions affecting adrenal function.</ARI_ClinicalSubtype>
        <ARI_ClinicalSubtype>Infectious Addison’s Disease - Resulting from infections like tuberculosis or fungal infections.</ARI_ClinicalSubtype>
        <ARI_DOID>13774</ARI_DOID>
        <ARI_DXCODE>363732003</ARI_DXCODE>
