        <ARI_Version>2.1</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>Anti-MDA5 dermatomyositis is a distinctive autoimmune inflammatory condition characterized by antibodies targeting melanoma differentiation-associated gene 5. Patients frequently present with typical skin findings and cutaneous ulcers with minimal muscle inflammation, but carry a substantial risk of developing rapidly progressive interstitial lung disease. Early, aggressive combined immunosuppressive therapy is critical to managing pulmonary complications. 60–70% of patients have a clinically amyopathic presentation with minimal muscle weakness.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Anti-MDA5 amyopathic dermatomyositis with rapidly progressive ILD</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


