        <ARI_PrevalenceDesc>Worldwide prevalence: 1.0 cases per 50 to 100. US prevalence: 1.0 cases per 50 to 100. Note on the US figure: Searched afterwards. Source: AHA / Circulation, calcific aortic valve disease in adults over 65.</ARI_PrevalenceDesc>
        <ARI_SNOMED>250978003</ARI_SNOMED>
        <ARI_UMLS>C0428791</ARI_UMLS>
        <ARI_Version>2.1</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>Autoinflammatory calcifying aortic valve disease is a chronic inflammatory disorder where innate immune cells infiltrate aortic valve tissue, triggering cytokine release and progressive fibrotic calcification. Over time, the aortic leaflets become stiff and restricted, leading to significant aortic stenosis and heart failure. Management focuses on monitoring hemodynamic progression and eventual surgical or transcatheter valve replacement.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Aortic valve calcification</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


