        <ARI_SurveyCode>ANG</ARI_SurveyCode>
        <ARI_SynonymWithdrawn>Acquired angiodema | broader | acquired angioedema (acquired C1-inhibitor deficiency) also covers the lymphoproliferative type I form, not only the autoimmune type II form</ARI_SynonymWithdrawn>
        <ARI_Version>2</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>Angioedema is swelling of the tissue just beneath the skin, including the face, lips, tongue, limbs, or genitals. People with Autoimmune Angioedema can have edema of the lining of the digestive tract, which can cause abdominal pain and nausea, as well as edema of the upper airway, which can be life-threatening.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Autoimmune angioedema</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


