        <ARI_Version>2.1</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>Autoimmune diabetes insipidus is a rare endocrine condition where autoantibodies or lymphocytic inflammation target the vasopressin-producing neurons of the hypothalamus and posterior pituitary gland. The resulting lack of antidiuretic hormone impairs the kidneys&apos; ability to concentrate urine, leading to excessive urination and intense thirst. Treatment involves hormone replacement with desmopressin alongside anti-inflammatory therapy.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Autoimmune diabetes insipidus (neurogenic)</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


