        <ARI_RefLink>Link to Healthline | https://www.healthline.com/health/atrophic-gastritis</ARI_RefLink>
        <ARI_RefLink>Pernicious Anemia Society | https://pernicious-anaemia-society.org/</ARI_RefLink>
        <ARI_SNOMED>84568007</ARI_SNOMED>
        <ARI_SurveyCode>AG</ARI_SurveyCode>
        <ARI_Synonym>Autoimmune atrophic gastritis</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_SynonymWithdrawn>Atrophic gastritis | broader | also covers H. pylori-associated multifocal atrophic gastritis; autoimmune gastritis is the corpus-restricted autoimmune form</ARI_SynonymWithdrawn>
        <ARI_SynonymWithdrawn>Autoimmune enteropathy | distinct | separate small-bowel disease with anti-enterocyte antibodies</ARI_SynonymWithdrawn>
        <ARI_SynonymWithdrawn>Eosinophilic gastritis | distinct | separate disease in the eosinophilic gastrointestinal disease spectrum</ARI_SynonymWithdrawn>
        <ARI_SynonymWithdrawn>Macrocytic Anemia | non-disease | downstream haematologic consequence of B12 deficiency, not a name for the gastritis</ARI_SynonymWithdrawn>
        <ARI_SynonymWithdrawn>Megaloblastic Anemia | non-disease | downstream haematologic consequence of B12 deficiency, not a name for the gastritis</ARI_SynonymWithdrawn>
        <ARI_UMLS>C3887639</ARI_UMLS>
        <ARI_Version>2</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>Autoimmune enteropathy is an extremely rare disease characterized by diarrhea that does not respond to treatment and may require intravenous feeding to sustain the patient. It is diagnosed most frequently in infants, and it is marked by the presence of antibodies to the enzyme tryptophan hydroxylase, which performs a number of functions in human biology,  Autoimmune enteropathy is increasingly being diagnosed in adults, but the symptoms are the same as many more common diseases, so correct diagnosis is difficult.   It is more frequently diagnosed in patients already diagnosed with other autoimmune diseases such as autoimmune polyendocrine syndrome 1.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Autoimmune gastritis</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


