        <ARI_SNOMED>237706000</ARI_SNOMED>
        <ARI_UMLS>C0342410</ARI_UMLS>
        <ARI_Version>2.1</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>Autoimmune hypophysitis is a chronic inflammatory disorder of the pituitary gland caused by autoimmune lymphocytic infiltration. Swelling of the pituitary stalk and gland can cause headaches and visual disturbances, while gland destruction leads to deficiencies in adrenal, thyroid, and sex hormones. It most commonly affects women during late pregnancy or postpartum, and treatment centers on corticosteroid therapy and hormone replacement.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Autoimmune hypophysitis</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


