        <ARI_MESH>D000099146</ARI_MESH>
        <ARI_Obsolete>false</ARI_Obsolete>
        <ARI_PrevalenceDesc>Worldwide prevalence: Extremely rare. US prevalence: Extremely rare. Note on the US figure: Searched afterwards. Source: Shoenfeld et al., adjuvant-induced autoimmune/inflammatory condition.</ARI_PrevalenceDesc>
        <ARI_Synonym>ASIA syndrome</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_UMLS>C5577685</ARI_UMLS>
        <ARI_Version>2.1</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>ASIA syndrome (autoimmune/autoinflammatory syndrome induced by adjuvants), also known as Shoenfeld&apos;s syndrome, describes a spectrum of immune-mediated conditions triggered by exposure to foreign adjuvants like silicone, mineral oil, or vaccines in genetically susceptible individuals. Clinical features include chronic fatigue, joint pain, muscle weakness, and autoantibody production. Management focuses on removing the inciting adjuvant and administering anti-inflammatory therapy.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Autoimmune-Inflammatory Syndrome Induced by Adjuvants</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


