        <ARI_UMLS>C2930824</ARI_UMLS>
        <ARI_Version>2.1</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>Seronegative autoimmune limbic encephalitis is an inflammatory disorder of the medial temporal lobes that occurs without detectable conventional antineuronal antibodies. Patients exhibit classic manifestations of limbic encephalitis, including subacute memory decline, seizures, and neuropsychiatric symptoms, with neuroimaging or CSF confirming inflammation. Empirical immunosuppressive treatment often leads to meaningful clinical improvement.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Autoimmune limbic encephalitis</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


