        <ARI_SNOMED>715863001</ARI_SNOMED>
        <ARI_Synonym>Immune-mediated necrotizing myopathy (IMNM)</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_UMLS>C3267047</ARI_UMLS>
        <ARI_Version>2.1</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>Immune-mediated necrotizing myopathy is a severe subtype of autoimmune myopathy marked by extensive muscle fiber necrosis with minimal lymphocytic inflammation. It is strongly linked to autoantibodies targeting signal recognition particle (anti-SRP) or HMG-CoA reductase (anti-HMGCR), the latter often triggered by statin exposure. Patients develop rapid proximal limb weakness and elevated creatine kinase, requiring aggressive immunosuppression. Serum creatine kinase is extremely elevated (&gt;10–50× the upper limit of normal) in 95–100% of patients, and 75–85% have no extramuscular systemic manifestations.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Autoimmune necrotizing myopathy</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


