        <ARI_SNOMED>707443007</ARI_SNOMED>
        <ARI_UMLS>C1970472</ARI_UMLS>
        <ARI_Version>2.1</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>Autoimmune pulmonary alveolar proteinosis is a rare lung disorder caused by neutralizing autoantibodies against granulocyte-macrophage colony-stimulating factor (GM-CSF). This antibody blocks alveolar macrophages from clearing surfactant, leading to the accumulation of lipoproteinaceous material within the alveoli and causing progressive breathlessness, cough, and hypoxia. Whole lung lavage and GM-CSF therapies are established treatments. Bronchoalveolar lavage returns milky, opaque fluid with PAS-positive proteinaceous material in 95–100% of patients.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Autoimmune pulmonary alveolar proteinosis</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


