        <rdfs:comment>Autoimmune retinopathy is a rare immune-mediated disorder in which autoantibodies attack retinal proteins, leading to progressive photoreceptor dysfunction. It is considered autoimmune even when no underlying trigger or associated systemic disease can be identified.</rdfs:comment>
