        <ARI_SynonymWithdrawn>Ocular pemphigoid | subtype | the eye-restricted form (ocular cicatricial pemphigoid); covered by existing subtype &quot;Benign Mucous Membrane Pemphigoid, Ocular&quot;</ARI_SynonymWithdrawn>
        <ARI_UMLS>C0030804</ARI_UMLS>
        <ARI_Version>2</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>Cicatricial pemphigoid is a rare autoimmune disease, discovered in 2002, that causes blistering of the mucous membranes. This blistering is due to autoantibodies binding to anchoring filaments of the epidermis.  A common mucous membrane that is affected is the conjunctiva of the eye.  Other areas that can be affected include the skin, nose, mouth, and genitals.

Cicatricial pemphigoid is usually not chronic, and most patients symptoms disappear within 3 years.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Benign mucous membrane pemphigoid</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


