        <ARI_Synonym>Bickerstaff encephalitis</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>Bickerstaff&apos;s encephalitis</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_UMLS>C1960543</ARI_UMLS>
        <ARI_Version>2.1</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>Bickerstaff brainstem encephalitis is a rare neuroinflammatory disorder within the anti-GQ1b antibody spectrum, characterized by autoantibodies targeting ganglioside GQ1b on cranial nerves and brainstem pathways. It classically presents with external ophthalmoplegia, ataxia, and altered consciousness or brisk reflexes. Prompt immunotherapy with intravenous immunoglobulin or plasma exchange generally yields substantial neurological recovery.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Bickerstaff&apos;s brainstem encephalitis</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


