        <ARI_ID>ARI:0001058</ARI_ID>
        <ARI_MONDO>0044113</ARI_MONDO>
        <ARI_NCI>C117104</ARI_NCI>
        <ARI_OMOP>4346976</ARI_OMOP>
        <ARI_Obsolete>false</ARI_Obsolete>
        <ARI_PrevalenceDesc>Worldwide prevalence: 1.0 cases per 500,000 to 1,000,000. US prevalence: 1.0 cases per 500,000 to 1,000,000. Note on the US figure: Searched afterwards. Source: Chan et al. / Lupus Foundation, rare vesiculobullous eruption in &lt;1-2% of SLE.</ARI_PrevalenceDesc>
        <ARI_SNOMED>239889005</ARI_SNOMED>
        <ARI_UMLS>C0409977</ARI_UMLS>
        <ARI_Version>2.1</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>Bullous systemic lupus erythematosus is an uncommon vesiculobullous manifestation of lupus erythematosus mediated by autoantibodies against type VII collagen at the dermal-epidermal junction. Patients develop widespread, tense blisters and erosions on sun-exposed and unexposed skin and mucous membranes. The condition responds rapidly to dapsone therapy, in addition to standard systemic lupus treatments. Biopsy shows a neutrophilic infiltrate at the dermal-epidermal junction in 95–100% of patients. Active systemic lupus manifestations accompany it, including lupus nephritis (50–60%) and arthritis (60–75%).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Bullous systemic lupus erythematosus</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


