        <ARI_UMLS>C3553512</ARI_UMLS>
        <ARI_Version>2.1</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>LRBA deficiency is a rare monogenic primary immunodeficiency and autoimmune disorder caused by biallelic loss-of-function mutations in the LRBA gene. The loss of LRBA accelerates CTLA-4 degradation in regulatory T cells, resulting in autoimmune cytopenias, inflammatory bowel disease, interstitial lung disease, and hypogammaglobulinemia. Targeted therapy using CTLA-4 mimetic agents (such as abatacept) significantly improves symptoms.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Combined immunodeficiency due to LRBA deficiency</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


