        <ARI_Obsolete>false</ARI_Obsolete>
        <ARI_PrevalenceDesc>Worldwide prevalence: 1.0 cases per 1,000,000; Extremely rare. US prevalence: Extremely rare. Note on the US figure: Searched afterwards. Source: Watkin et al. / NORD, rare hereditary autoimmune pulmonary-renal syndrome.</ARI_PrevalenceDesc>
        <ARI_SNOMED>1222679006</ARI_SNOMED>
        <ARI_Synonym>Autoimmune interstitial lung disease-arthritis syndrome</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>autoimmune interstitial lung, joint, and kidney disease</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>autoinflammation and autoimmunity, Systemic with immune dysregulation</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>systemic autoinflammation and autoimmunity with immune dysregulation 1</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_UMLS>C5243948</ARI_UMLS>
        <ARI_Version>2.1</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>COPA syndrome is a monogenic autoinflammatory and autoimmune disorder caused by mutations in the COPA gene, which impairs intracellular retrograde Golgi-to-ER protein trafficking and activates the STING pathway. Manifestations include early-onset interstitial lung disease, pulmonary hemorrhage, arthritis, and glomerulonephritis. Management involves targeted immunomodulation, including JAK inhibitors and immunosuppressive agents.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>COPA syndrome</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


