        <ARI_PrevalenceDesc>Worldwide prevalence: 1.0 cases per 1,000,000; Extremely rare. US prevalence: Extremely rare. Note on the US figure: Searched afterwards. Source: Kuehn et al. / Schwab et al., primary immune deficiency with immune dysregulation.</ARI_PrevalenceDesc>
        <ARI_SNOMED>1197361002</ARI_SNOMED>
        <ARI_UMLS>C4015214</ARI_UMLS>
        <ARI_Version>2.1</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>CTLA4 haploinsufficiency is an inherited immune dysregulation syndrome caused by heterozygous mutations in the CTLA4 gene, which diminishes regulatory T-cell suppressive capacity. This leads to widespread immune cell proliferation and multiorgan autoimmunity, including enteropathy, cytopenias, respiratory disease, and hypogammaglobulinemia. Targeted treatment with CTLA-4 fusion proteins (such as abatacept) provides substantial clinical benefit.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>CTLA4 haploinsufficiency</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


