        <ARI_Pubmed>https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8276524/</ARI_Pubmed>
        <ARI_SNOMED>414238007</ARI_SNOMED>
        <ARI_Synonym>Infertility due to antisperm antibodies</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_UMLS>C1531958</ARI_UMLS>
        <ARI_Version>2</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>Anti-sperm antibodies (ASA) is a lab measurement, not a disease, but a high level of ASA may point to an autoimmune condition.

In women, ASA is an allergic response that can be an immunologic cause of infertility. 

ASA is not a concern except for people trying to conceive. Findings include a severely abnormal post-coital test, with poor sperm motility and survival in cervical mucus (75–85%), and impaired sperm-egg binding with fertilization failure during IVF (60–75%).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Female infertility due to antisperm antibodies</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


