        <rdfs:comment>Primary membranous nephropathy is an autoimmune kidney disease and a leading cause of nephrotic syndrome in adults, characterized by autoantibodies targeting antigens on podocytes, predominantly the M-type phospholipase A2 receptor (PLA2R). Immune complex deposition in the subepithelial space damages the glomerular basement membrane, causing severe proteinuria. Treatments include immunosuppressive therapy with rituximab or alkylating agents.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Idiopathic membranous glomerulonephritis</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


