        <rdfs:comment>A kidney disease that occurs when the antibody immunoglobulin A lodges in the kidneys.  In IgA nephropathy, the antibodies do not attack tissue directly, but they do cause inflammation that can inhibit the kidneys&apos; ability to filter wastes from the blood over time.  ARI classifies IgA nephropathy as immune-related, not autoimmune.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>IgA nephropathy</rdfs:label>
