        <ARI_Synonym>IgG4-related ophthalmic disease</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_UMLS>C5569009</ARI_UMLS>
        <ARI_Version>2.1</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>IgG4-related ophthalmic disease is a fibro-inflammatory condition affecting orbital tissues, most frequently the lacrimal glands, extraocular muscles, and orbital fat, within the IgG4-related disease spectrum. Patients present with painless orbital swelling, proptosis, or double vision, accompanied by dense IgG4-positive plasma cell infiltration and tissue fibrosis. Corticosteroids and B-cell depletion therapy are highly effective therapies.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Immunoglobulin G4 related ophthalmic disease</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


