        <ARI_SNOMED>408539000</ARI_SNOMED>
        <ARI_Synonym>Hirata disease</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>Hirata syndrome</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_UMLS>C0854359</ARI_UMLS>
        <ARI_Version>2.1</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>Insulin autoimmune syndrome, or Hirata disease, is a rare autoimmune disorder characterized by spontaneous, severe hypoglycemia caused by high levels of polyclonal autoantibodies directed against endogenous insulin. The antibodies bind insulin post-prandially and later release it unpredictably into the bloodstream, triggering severe drops in blood sugar. It is strongly linked to specific HLA alleles and sulfhydryl-containing medications. 70–80% of patients have a spontaneous clinical remission within 3–6 months.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Insulin autoimmune syndrome</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


