        <ARI_SNOMED>237652003</ARI_SNOMED>
        <ARI_Synonym>Type B insulin resistance syndrome</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_UMLS>C0342337</ARI_UMLS>
        <ARI_Version>2.1</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>Type B insulin resistance syndrome is an extremely rare, severe autoimmune disorder caused by autoantibodies directed against the insulin receptor. These antibodies block insulin action, causing extreme hyperglycemia and acanthosis nigricans, or periodically stimulate receptors causing severe paradoxical hypoglycemia. The disease is frequently associated with systemic lupus erythematosus and is treated with combination immunotherapy.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Insulin resistance - type B</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


