        <ARI_Version>2</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>Interstitial lung disease is a small group of diseases that feature inflammation and the development of fibrous tissue that affects the small airways and the small sacks in the lungs (alveoli) where oxygen is exchanged for carbon dioxide. The two most common diseases in this group are idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis and cryptogenic organizing pneumonia, both of which can occur as “idiopathic” conditions (where the cause is unknown) or in association with several autoimmune diseases. Although both are classified as “lung disorders of unknown etiology,” there are clues that autoimmune mechanisms play a role in the development of both disorders.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Interstitial lung disease</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


