        <ARI_PrevalenceDesc>Worldwide incidence: 1.0 cases per 10,000,000; Extremely rare. US incidence: 1.0 cases per 10,000,000 (Extremely rare). Note on the US figure: Searched afterwards. Source: Balint et al. / PubMed, extremely rare synaptic encephalitis.</ARI_PrevalenceDesc>
        <ARI_SNOMED>773395008</ARI_SNOMED>
        <ARI_UMLS>C4750833</ARI_UMLS>
        <ARI_Version>2.1</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>Anti-DPPX encephalitis is an autoimmune encephalopathy caused by autoantibodies directed against dipeptidyl-peptidase-like protein-6, an auxiliary subunit of neuronal potassium channels. Patients experience central nervous system hyperexcitability, prominent cognitive difficulties, tremors, hallucinations, and severe gastrointestinal symptoms such as diarrhea and profound weight loss. Early identification and prompt immunosuppressive therapy can lead to substantial clinical recovery.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Limbic encephalitis with dipeptidyl-peptidase 6 antibodies</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


