        <ARI_ClinicalSubtype>Mixed Collagen Vascular Disease, Overlap Syndrome - Features from multiple autoimmune diseases.</ARI_ClinicalSubtype>
        <ARI_DOID>3492</ARI_DOID>
        <ARI_DXCODE>398049005</ARI_DXCODE>
        <ARI_DefSource>Gunnarsson 2011; https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21398332/</ARI_DefSource>
        <ARI_ICD10>M35.1</ARI_ICD10>
        <ARI_ID>ARI:0001130</ARI_ID>
        <ARI_MESH>D008947</ARI_MESH>
        <ARI_MONDO>0005854</ARI_MONDO>
        <ARI_NCI>C84892</ARI_NCI>
        <ARI_OMOP>4134867</ARI_OMOP>
        <ARI_ORPHANET>809</ARI_ORPHANET>
        <ARI_Obsolete>false</ARI_Obsolete>
        <ARI_PrevalenceDesc>Worldwide prevalence: 1.0 cases per 25,000 to 50,000. US prevalence: 1.0 cases per 22,727 to 31,250.</ARI_PrevalenceDesc>
        <ARI_Pubmed>https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21398332/</ARI_Pubmed>
        <ARI_RefLink>A twist of fate: Living with MCTD | http://atofclt.weebly.com/</ARI_RefLink>
        <ARI_RefLink>Link to Cleveland Clinic | https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/24342-collagen-vascular-disease</ARI_RefLink>
        <ARI_RefLink>Link to Healthline | https://www.healthline.com/health/collagen-vascular-disease</ARI_RefLink>
        <ARI_RefLink>MCTD - The Truth, the Challenge and the Hope | https://mctd.wordpress.com/</ARI_RefLink>
        <ARI_RefLink>MCTD Foundation | http://mctdfoundation.org/</ARI_RefLink>
        <ARI_RefLink>The Tube-Fed Wife | https://thetubefedwife.blogspot.com/</ARI_RefLink>
        <ARI_SNOMED>398049005</ARI_SNOMED>
        <ARI_SurveyCode>MCVD</ARI_SurveyCode>
        <ARI_Synonym>MCTD</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>Mixed connective tissue disease</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>Sharp Syndrome</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_UMLS>C0026272</ARI_UMLS>
        <ARI_Version>2</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>Mixed collagen vascular disease, also called mixed connective tissue disease (MCTD), is an autoimmune disorder that shares symptoms with other connective tissue diseases, including polymyositis/dermatomyositis, systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE), scleroderma, and autoimmune rheumatic diseases.  Examples of commonly shared symptoms are abnormally cold hands, joint pain, organ problems, and feelings of malaise.  However, one feature unique to MCTD is the presence of anti-RNP antibodies in the blood.  Raynaud&apos;s phenomenon and high blood pressure in the lungs are also more common in MCTD, while kidney symptoms are milder.  Some complications can be fatal, but treatments are available to manage both mild and life-threatening symptoms.   [Hajas et al., 2013].</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Mixed collagen vascular disease</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


