        <ARI_SNOMED>95609003</ARI_SNOMED>
        <ARI_SynonymWithdrawn>Congenital heart block due to maternal anti-Ro/SSA and anti-La/SSB | subtype | the cardiac manifestation of neonatal lupus (~2% of cases); neonatal lupus also presents as rash, cytopenias or hepatitis, often without heart block</ARI_SynonymWithdrawn>
        <ARI_UMLS>C0409979</ARI_UMLS>
        <ARI_Version>2.1</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>Neonatal lupus is a passively acquired autoimmune condition where maternal IgG autoantibodies against Ro/SSA and La/SSB cross the placenta and affect fetal tissues. The most serious consequence is irreversible congenital complete heart block caused by inflammation and fibrosis of the fetal cardiac conduction system, while cutaneous rashes and liver enzyme abnormalities are typically transient and resolve as maternal antibodies clear.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Neonatal lupus erythematosus</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


