        <ARI_PrevalenceDesc>Worldwide prevalence: 1.0 cases per 1,000,000; Extremely rare. US prevalence: Extremely rare. Note on the US figure: Searched afterwards. Source: Anhalt et al. / NORD, ultra-rare autoimmune bullous disease.</ARI_PrevalenceDesc>
        <ARI_UMLS>C1112570</ARI_UMLS>
        <ARI_Version>2.1</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>Paraneoplastic pemphigus, also known as paraneoplastic autoimmune multiorgan syndrome (PAMS), is a severe blistering disorder associated with underlying neoplasms like lymphoma or Castleman disease. Autoantibodies target plakin family proteins and desmogleins, causing intractable mucosal ulcerations, polymorphic cutaneous lesions, and lethal bronchiolitis obliterans. Treatment requires eradicating the neoplasm and administering intensive immunosuppression.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Paraneoplastic pemphigus</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


