        <ARI_PrevalenceDesc>Worldwide prevalence: 1.0 cases per 500,000 to 1,000,000. US prevalence: 1.0 cases per 500,000 to 1,000,000. Note on the US figure: Searched afterwards. Source: NORD / ASH, rare autoimmune hemolytic anemia (&lt;1-2% of AIHA).</ARI_PrevalenceDesc>
        <ARI_SNOMED>127057004</ARI_SNOMED>
        <ARI_UMLS>C0086774</ARI_UMLS>
        <ARI_Version>2.1</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>Paroxysmal cold hemoglobinuria is a rare autoimmune hemolytic anemia caused by the Donath-Landsteiner autoantibody, an IgG antibody that binds red blood cells at cold temperatures and fixes complement. Rewarming to normal body temperature causes intravascular hemolysis, leading to dark red urine (hemoglobinuria), fatigue, and jaundice. It most commonly follows viral respiratory infections in children and typically resolves spontaneously.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Paroxysmal cold hemoglobinuria</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


