        <ARI_Version>2</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>Polyglandular autoimmune syndrome type 1 is a rare autoimmune condition that is caused by a genetic variant that prevents the destruction of antibodies in the thymus gland. As a result, those antibodies attack healthy tissue in a number of glands, leading to the symptoms. There are three components of APECED: chronic mucocutaneous candidiasis, hypoparathyroidism, and adrenal insufficiency.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Polyglandular autoimmune syndrome type 1</rdfs:label>
