        <ARI_SurveyCode>PM</ARI_SurveyCode>
        <ARI_UMLS>C0085655</ARI_UMLS>
        <ARI_Version>2</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>Polymyositis is inflammation of muscle tissue, causing chronic muscle weakness in both sides of the body. This results in mobility issues, such as difficulty climbing stairs, rising from a seated position, lifting objects, etc. Polymyositis mostly affects adults ages 30 to 50s, and women are usually more often affected compared to men. This disease develops gradually, affecting both sides of the muscles closest to the trunk, such as the hips, neck, upper arms, and thighs. The risk of polymyositis increases if already diagnosed with another autoimmune disease, for example, lupus, rheumatoid arthritis, scleroderma, or Sjogren’s syndrome.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Polymyositis</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


