        <ARI_UMLS>C1449563</ARI_UMLS>
        <ARI_Version>2</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>A disease in which the immune system attacks the heart muscle causing inflammation, normally beginning in the heart&apos;s left ventricle (the heart&apos;s main pumping chamber). The ventricle stretches and thins and is unable to pump blood as a healthy heart can. Not all patients experience symptoms, but for some it can be life-threatening.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Primary idiopathic dilated cardiomyopathy</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


