        <ARI_ClinicalSubtype>Sympathetic Uveitis, Classic - Bilateral eye inflammation after trauma or surgery.</ARI_ClinicalSubtype>
        <ARI_DOID>12029</ARI_DOID>
        <ARI_DXCODE>75315001</ARI_DXCODE>
        <ARI_DefSource>Arevalo 2012; https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3277011/</ARI_DefSource>
        <ARI_ICD10>H44.13</ARI_ICD10>
        <ARI_ID>ARI:0001195</ARI_ID>
        <ARI_MESH>D009879</ARI_MESH>
        <ARI_MONDO>0019198</ARI_MONDO>
        <ARI_OMOP>438739</ARI_OMOP>
        <ARI_ORPHANET>79098</ARI_ORPHANET>
        <ARI_Obsolete>false</ARI_Obsolete>
        <ARI_PrevalenceDesc>Worldwide prevalence: 1.0 cases per 1,000,000 to 3,000,000. US incidence: 1.0 cases per 3,333,333.</ARI_PrevalenceDesc>
        <ARI_RefLink>Olivia’s Vision | http://www.oliviasvision.org/</ARI_RefLink>
        <ARI_RefLink>The Ocular Immunology and Uveitis Foundation | https://uveitis.org/</ARI_RefLink>
        <ARI_RefLink>Uveitis Online Support Group | https://www.tapatalk.com/groups/uveitissupport/</ARI_RefLink>
        <ARI_SNOMED>75315001</ARI_SNOMED>
        <ARI_SurveyCode>SU</ARI_SurveyCode>
        <ARI_Synonym>Sympathetic ophthalmia</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_SynonymWithdrawn>Exciting Eye | non-disease | labels for the injured and fellow eyes, not names of the disease</ARI_SynonymWithdrawn>
        <ARI_SynonymWithdrawn>Spared Eye Injury | non-disease | labels for the injured and fellow eyes, not names of the disease</ARI_SynonymWithdrawn>
        <ARI_SynonymWithdrawn>Sympathizing Eye | non-disease | labels for the injured and fellow eyes, not names of the disease</ARI_SynonymWithdrawn>
        <ARI_UMLS>C0029077</ARI_UMLS>
        <ARI_Version>2</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>Sympathetic Ophthalmia (SO) is a rare inflammatory condition that affects both eyes following trauma or surgery to one of the eyes. The immune system is sensitized to proteins from the damaged eye and then attacks those same proteins in the uninjured (or “spared” eye), leading to inflammation of the uninjured eye. Sympathetic ophthalmia is a form of uveitis. The disease can lead to blindness.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Sympathetic uveitis</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


