        <rdfs:comment>Temporal arteritis, also known as giant cell arteritis, is an inflammation of the lining of the arteries that typically affects the arteries in the head. Temporal arteritis can frequently cause headaches, scalp tenderness, jaw pain and vision problems.</rdfs:comment>
