        <ARI_SynonymWithdrawn>Cancer-associated myositis | broader | cancer-associated myositis also covers anti-NXP2 and seronegative cases, and not all anti-TIF1-gamma patients have cancer; a broader category</ARI_SynonymWithdrawn>
        <ARI_Version>2.1</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>Anti-TIF1-gamma dermatomyositis is a subtype of dermatomyositis defined by autoantibodies directed against transcriptional intermediary factor 1-gamma. It is characterized by extensive, severe photosensitive skin rashes and proximal muscle weakness, and is strongly associated with an elevated risk of underlying malignancy in adult patients. Management requires comprehensive age-appropriate cancer screening and targeted immunosuppressive regimens. The risk of internal malignancy within 3 years of diagnosis is very high (50–70%).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>TIF1-gamma positive dermatomyositis</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


