        <ARI_Synonym>AMPA receptor antibody encephalitis</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>AMPA receptor limbic encephalitis</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>AMPAR antibody encephalitis</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>AMPAR antibody-associated autoimmune encephalitis</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>anti-GluA1 encephalitis</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>anti-GluA2 encephalitis</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>anti-GluR1/GluR2 encephalitis</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>anti-alpha-amino-3-hydroxy-5-methyl-4-isoxazolepropionic acid receptor encephalitis</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>autoimmune encephalitis with AMPAR antibodies</ARI_Synonym>
        <rdfs:comment>Anti-AMPAR encephalitis is a rare autoimmune disorder of the central nervous system in which autoantibodies attack the GluA1 or GluA2 subunits of AMPA glutamate receptors in the brain. This disrupts synaptic signaling, leading to limbic encephalitis characterized by rapid memory loss, confusion, behavioral changes, and seizures. A significant number of cases occur as a paraneoplastic syndrome associated with underlying tumors, and patients typically benefit from early immunomodulatory treatment.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Anti-AMPAR encephalitis</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


