        <ARI_Synonym>Anti-GABA-B receptor encephalitis</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>GABAB receptor antibody encephalitis</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>GABABR limbic encephalitis</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>GABA_B receptor encephalitis</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>anti-GABAB receptor encephalitis</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>anti-GABAB-R encephalitis</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>anti-gamma-aminobutyric acid B receptor encephalitis</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>autoimmune encephalitis with anti-GABAB receptor antibodies</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>paraneoplastic anti-GABAB receptor encephalitis</ARI_Synonym>
        <rdfs:comment>Anti-GABA B receptor encephalitis is an autoimmune limbic encephalitis caused by autoantibodies directed against inhibitory GABA_B receptors in the brain. Patients typically present with prominent temporal lobe seizures, acute memory deficits, and psychiatric changes. The condition is frequently paraneoplastic, strongly associated with small cell lung cancer, and management involves targeted oncological treatment and immunomodulatory therapy.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Anti-GABA B encephalitis</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


