        <rdfs:comment>Autoimmune GFAP astrocytopathy is an inflammatory central nervous system condition defined by autoantibodies directed against glial fibrillary acidic protein in astrocytes. Patients often present with meningoencephalomyelitis, displaying fever, headache, cognitive changes, optic disc swelling, and ataxia, accompanied by distinctive perivascular enhancement on brain MRI. It typically shows excellent clinical response to corticosteroid therapy.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Autoimmune GFAP astrocytopathy</rdfs:label>
