        <ARI_Synonym>nodal antibody neuropathy</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>paranodal antibody neuropathy</ARI_Synonym>
        <rdfs:comment>Autoimmune peripheral neuropathy associated with nodal and paranodal antibodies is a specialized neuropathy subtype where autoantibodies attack proteins maintaining the axoglial junctions of peripheral nerves. Patients develop subacute to chronic motor and sensory deficits, marked limb weakness, and gait unsteadiness. Identification of specific nodal antibodies directs physicians toward tailored immunosuppressive options such as rituximab.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Autoimmune peripheral neuropathy associated with nodal/paranodal antibodies</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


