        <ARI_Synonym>ADAMTS13 inhibitor-associated TTP</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>aTTP</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>acquired TTP</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>acquired severe ADAMTS13 deficiency</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>acquired thrombotic thrombocytopenic purpura</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>anti-ADAMTS13 antibody-mediated TTP</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>autoimmune thrombotic thrombocytopenic purpura</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>iTTP</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>immune TTP</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>immune-mediated TTP</ARI_Synonym>
        <rdfs:comment>Immune-mediated thrombotic thrombocytopenic purpura is a life-threatening hematologic emergency caused by autoantibodies inhibiting the ADAMTS13 enzyme. Without functional ADAMTS13, ultra-large von Willebrand factor multimers accumulate and induce widespread microvascular blood clots, hemolytic anemia, and thrombocytopenia. Immediate treatment involves therapeutic plasma exchange, immunosuppressive therapy, and anti-vWF nanobodies.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Immune-mediated thrombotic thrombocytopenic purpura (iTTP)</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


