        <ARI_Synonym>Kleine-Levin syndrome</ARI_Synonym>
        <rdfs:comment>Kleine-Levin syndrome is a rare neurological disorder characterized by recurring episodes of extreme hypersomnia accompanied by cognitive impairment, behavioral changes, and hyperphagia. While suspected immune and hypothalamic mechanisms have been proposed, clear autoantibody markers remain unconfirmed, and it is classified as an unconfirmed autoimmune condition. Management focuses on supportive care and mood-stabilizing medications during episodes. Cognition, sleep and mood are completely normal between episodes (100%).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Klein Levin Syndrome</rdfs:label>
