        <ARI_Synonym>STAT3 GOF syndrome</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>STAT3 gain-of-function syndrome</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>STAT3-GOF disease</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>STAT3-associated immune dysregulation</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>early-onset lymphoproliferation and autoimmunity due to STAT3 gain-of-function mutations</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>early-onset multiorgan autoimmunity due to STAT3 GOF</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>germline STAT3 GOF disease</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>infantile-onset multisystem autoimmune disease due to STAT3 GOF</ARI_Synonym>
        <ARI_Synonym>monogenic early-onset lymphoproliferation and autoimmunity</ARI_Synonym>
        <rdfs:comment>STAT3 gain-of-function disease is a monogenic autoimmune disorder caused by activating mutations in the STAT3 gene, which leads to constitutive transcriptional activation and widespread immune dysregulation. Patients present in early childhood with multiorgan autoimmunity, including type 1 diabetes, autoimmune enteropathy, interstitial lung disease, and short stature. Targeted therapy with JAK inhibitors has shown promising efficacy.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>STAT3 gain-of-function disease</rdfs:label>
